WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.531
A detection is confirmed, so now we issue the ticket.

2
00:00:04.531 --> 00:00:07.182
That is Performance Criterion 1.5.

3
00:00:07.182 --> 00:00:10.924
A ticket is the official record of one incident.

4
00:00:10.924 --> 00:00:17.394
It must contain every alert and report about that incident, and facts, not guesses.

5
00:00:17.394 --> 00:00:22.696
I will write the ticket for the ransomware on the school library PC.

6
00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:25.518
First the template.

7
00:00:25.518 --> 00:00:34.675
Ticket ID, title, opened, linked alerts, affected asset, category, priority, evidence, actions taken,

8
00:00:34.675 --> 00:00:36.851
assigned to, and status.

9
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:45.247
Rule T2 says one ticket per incident, so I collect everything about LIB-PC-02.

10
00:00:45.247 --> 00:00:48.427
In the queue there are two alerts.

11
00:00:48.427 --> 00:00:50.765
D5-02 is the ransom note.

12
00:00:50.765 --> 00:00:57.967
D5-06 is the agent keep-alive, routine, so it does not belong on this ticket.

13
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:07.487
The details of D5-02 give me the evidence: five files renamed to dot crypt nine by winhelper dot exe,

14
00:01:07.487 --> 00:01:09.987
unsigned, and the ransom note.

15
00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:16.128
And the librarian's phone call, report DR-1, is about the same PC.

16
00:01:16.128 --> 00:01:18.571
It is linked to the same ticket.

17
00:01:18.571 --> 00:01:26.666
During that call I told her to unplug the network cable and not to shut down, and I phoned the Shift Lead.

18
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:28.727
Those are my actions taken.

19
00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:32.034
Here is the finished ticket.

20
00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:36.052
Critical threat, so P1, assigned to the Shift Lead.

21
00:01:36.052 --> 00:01:42.198
Status New: Level I opens and hands over, and never closes an incident ticket.

22
00:01:42.198 --> 00:01:50.707
Notice what is not in it: no passwords, and only the personal data we need, because of the Data Privacy Act.

23
00:01:51.807 --> 00:01:52.712
Your turn.

24
00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:56.057
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 6.

25
00:01:56.057 --> 00:02:06.366
In Activity 6.3, issue the ticket for the ransomware on FIN-PC-03: find every alert and the report about it first.

26
00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:12.605
Then in Activity 6.4, triage the five alerts on your own workstation.

27
00:02:12.605 --> 00:02:14.776
Every seat is different.

